.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-container-get - Container environment detail (namespace, internal addressing, egress IPs)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro container get  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Container environment detail (namespace, internal addressing, egress IPs)

.PP
Environment code, Kubernetes \fBnamespace\fP, in-cluster addressing (\fBcluster_dns\fR), plan limits, nodes, quota, ingress IPs and the current \fBegress IPs\fP\&. Egress IPs of a \fBdedicated\fP environment = the public IPs of its own nodes + the shared pool node(s) used while an update rolls out (the new copy starts there for about a minute, then moves back to your node). \fBServerless\fP = the shared sandboxed pool nodes (the pool can grow: a new address can appear). Build machines of Gyro Pipeline are listed separately (\fBbuild_ips\fR). The list changes when the nodes change (plan change, node replacement, pool scaling); the owner is notified (Alerts channels, event \fBegress\fR). No IPv6 egress; outbound TCP 25 is closed. A fixed egress address is not offered yet.

.PP
API: GET /cloud/containers/{id} (operationId getContainerEnvironment, scope services_read)


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for get


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	API base URL (env GYRO_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	log HTTP requests to stderr (secrets masked)

.PP
\fB--lang\fP=""
	message language: tr or en (default from locale)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-header\fP[=false]
	omit the table header

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	output format: table, json, yaml, text

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (env GYRO_PROFILE)

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath query applied to the result

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	print only ids

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=0s
	overall timeout, e.g. 30s, 10m

.PP
\fB--wide\fP[=false]
	show all table columns

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
